                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A stripped-down blackjack game where you win outfits off your opponent. It doesn't deliver what the store page promises.\n\n1. The store page advertises naked breasts. There are none. Everything stays in underwear — no nudity, no scenes at all.\n2. The adult content is just a skin swap: the same idle animation throughout, only the outfit changes.\n3. The character model is plastic. It looks like it was made in an old version of Unity, animation included, and she smiles with an enormous unnatural grin that lands closer to unsettling than attractive.\n4. The art direction itself I actually like — it has its own vibe.\n5. The character's figure is well done.\n6. Pleasant, simple gameplay.\n7. The blackjack is bare-bones: hit and stand, nothing else. No doubling, no splitting, no betting decisions.\n8. The randomness feels rigged. I played optimal strategy and still kept losing — two hours of it for a single outfit, and there are only three or four in total.\n9. The sound effects are dumb. The music is fine on its own, but combined with everything above it wears out fast.\n10. I quit after unlocking one costume. Grinding hours for the rest wasn't worth it.\n11. The price is too high at 200 rub. I'd put it at 50-100.\n\nThe game could have been genuinely appealing. What it needs is actual adult content, polish, and mechanics worth playing.",
